        jobs.add(new JobAd("Fullstack Developer (f/m/d)", "You have a passion for technology and want to make the world a greener place?Then become a changemaker (f/m/d) and join our team as Fullstack Developer (f/m/d) at E.ON Digital Technology (EDT).E.ON Digital Technology plays a key role in shaping the energy transition by leading E.ON’s digital transformation across Europe. We explore new paths through developing ideas, breaking new ground, making visions reality, and bringing new technologies to life. In flexible working models and teams, we deliver sustainable technology solutions to meet the energy challenges of tomorrow.meaningful & challenging – Your tasksAdvise business partners from both functional and technical perspectives on the conceptual design of digital solutionsDevelop source code for digital solutions based on user stories, covering both frontend and backendPlan user stories and estimate the implementation effortShare up-to-date market and technology trends, contributing your knowledge to projects and peersActively participate in team decisions and drive changeBe part of a highly motivated team, working on international projects with an impact on the energy industryWe are seeking individuals for our team who embody a 'can-do' attitude and a passion for learning. Skills can be acquired and honed with dedication, a positive attitude and a growth mindset are the foundation for success in our organization.authentic & ambitious – Your profileSeveral years of experience in software development, including software architecture models and concepts such as microservices or service-oriented architecture, as well as domain-driven designDeep technical understanding with the ability to translate business requirements into softwareProficient in backend development using object-oriented languages like Java, Kotlin, C#, or Go, and familiar with backend frameworks like Spring Boot or NodeJSSkilled in frontend technologies, including Angular or React, TypeScript, HTML/CSS, (S)CSS, and accessibility guidelinesExperienced with cloud services (Azure) and scalable cloud computing systemsProficient in DevOps tools and agile enablement tools (JIRA, Confluence, Miro)Strong team player capable of working with diverse, international groups in a productive and agile mannerVery good English skills and basic German skills, with a willingness to travel approximately twice per monthsmart & useful – Our benefitsWe provide full flexibility: Do your work from home or any other place in Germany - of course including all our great offices from Hamburg to Munich. You want even more? Go on workation for up to 20 days per year within Europe.Recharge your battery: You have 30 holidays per year plus Christmas and New Year´s Eve on top. Your battery still needs charging? You can exchange parts of your salary for more holidays or you can take a sabbatical.Your development: We grow and we want you to grow with us. Learning on the job, exchanging with other or taking part in an individual training - Our learning culture enables you to bring your personal and professional development to the next level.We elevate your mobility: From car and bike leasing offers to job tickets for most of our locations– your way is our way.We also think ahead: With our company retirements scheme and a great insurance package we take care of your future.This is by far not all: We are looking forward to speaking with you about further benefits during the recruiting process.Do you have questions?For further information please contact Stephan Fiedler, stephan.fiedler@eon.com.Please understand that for data protection reasons we can only accept applications submitted via our portal. Unfortunately, we cannot consider application documents that reach us by email or post.What you need to know:Job Req ID: 230351Contract type: PermanentWorking time: Part or Full timeCompany: E.ON Digital Technology GmbHLocation: Essen, Hannover, Würzburg, München, Berlin, Hamburg, Frankfurt am MainFunction area: Engineering", "E.ON Digital Technology", "https://de.linkedin.com/jobs/view/fullstack-developer-f-m-d-at-e-on-digital-technology-4024837450?trk=public_jobs_topcard-title", "Munich, Bavaria, Germany"));
